From: Senemos Uke maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] iio: adc: expose Gen3 charger current and battery temperature

Port PMIC7 charger temperature, signed IIN_FB and ICHG_FB conversions and the
Gen3 battery 100k resistance curve from Qualcomm's Uke downstream driver.
Normalize current to the processed IIO mA ABI and battery decidegrees to mC.
Select the distinct battery curve with a documented channel property, rather
than importing downstream private enum numbers into the upstream ABI.

Source: MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource
Commit: 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd
Files: drivers/iio/adc/qcom-vadc-common.c, qcom-spmi-adc5-gen3.c
License: GPL-2.0-only; retain upstream Qualcomm attribution.
Cross-check: OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm7675, fc892483f1d61f245924681eb5abd563564d9cba.
The selected four formulas/table agree; unrelated Oplus curves are not copied.
No charging limit, thermal trip, calibration storage or firmware is changed.

